| As of 2024, three cantons have official minimum salaries: {{Currency|20.60|CHF}} (US${{to USD|20.60|CHE|round=no}}) per hour in the [[Cantons of Switzerland|canton]] of [[Canton of Jura|Jura]]; {{Currency|21.09|CHF}} (US${{to USD|21.09|CHE|round=no}}) per hour in the canton of [[Canton of Neuchâtel|Neuchâtel]], {{Currency|24.32|CHF}} (US${{to USD|24.32|CHE|round=no}}) in the canton of [[Canton of Geneva|Geneva]];<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.ge.ch/appliquer-salaire-minimum-genevois/montant-calcul-du-salaire-minimum#:~:text=Depuis%20le%201er%20janvier%202024,heure%20au%201er%20janvier%202023 | title=Montant et calcul du salaire minimum | date=17 Oct 2023 | access-date=3 Mar 2024 | archive-date=3 Mar 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240303195050/https://www.ge.ch/appliquer-salaire-minimum-genevois/montant-calcul-du-salaire-minimum#:~:text=Depuis%20le%201er%20janvier%202024,heure%20au%201er%20janvier%202023 | url-status=live }}</ref> the rest of the country has no minimum wage.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.thelocal.ch/20171123/jura-parliament-finally-agrees-minimum-wage-of-20-francs-per-hour|title=Jura parliament finally agrees minimum wage of 20 francs per hour|date=23 Nov 2017|access-date=28 Nov 2017|language=en|archive-date=1 Dec 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171201035859/https://www.thelocal.ch/20171123/jura-parliament-finally-agrees-minimum-wage-of-20-francs-per-hour|url-status=live}}</ref> There are a minority of the voluntary ''General Labour Contracts'' (GLC, collective labour agreements), reached on a sector-by-sector basis,<ref>{{cite web| url=http://www.seco.admin.ch/themen/00385/00420/00430/index.html| title=Allgemeinverbindlicherklärung von Gesamtarbeitsverträgen| publisher=Swiss State Secretariat for Economic Affairs SECO, Swiss Federal Department of Economic Affairs, Education and Research EAER| location=Neuchâtel| date=1 May 2014| language=de, fr, it| access-date=20 May 2014| archive-date=20 May 2014| archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140520220517/http://www.seco.admin.ch/themen/00385/00420/00430/index.html| url-status=live}}</ref> contain minimum compensation clauses, which provide for compensation ranging from {{Currency|2,200|CHF|linked=no}} to {{Currency|4,200|CHF|linked=no}} (US${{to USD|2200|CHE|round=yes}} to US${{to USD|4200|CHE|round=yes}}) per month for unskilled workers and {{Currency|2,800|CHF|linked=no}} to {{Currency|5,300|CHF|linked=no}} (US${{to USD|2800|CHE|round=yes}} to US${{to USD|5300|CHE|round=yes}}) per month for skilled employees.<ref name="CRHRP-2012" /> On 18 May 2014, Swiss voters rejected a federal [[Referendums by country#Switzerland|initiative]] (by 76.3%) that would have enforced ''GLCs'' for every sector and set the hourly minimum wage at {{Currency|22|CHF|linked=no}} (US${{to USD|22|CHE|round=no}}, or [[Purchasing power parity|PPP]]-adjusted US$12.55).<ref>{{cite news|last=Eddy|first=Melissa|title=Swiss Defeat Minimum Wage by Large Margin|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/business/international/swiss-defeat-minimum-wage-by-large-margin.html|access-date=18 May 2014|newspaper=New York Times|date=18 May 2014|archive-date=19 May 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140519015918/http://www.nytimes.com/2014/05/19/business/international/swiss-defeat-minimum-wage-by-large-margin.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web| url=http://www.bfs.admin.ch/bfs/portal/de/index/themen/17/03/blank/key/2014/023.html| title=Abstimmungen – Indikatoren, Abstimmung vom 18. Mai 2014: Mindestlohn-Initiative| publisher=Swiss Federal Office of Statistics, Swiss Federal Administration| location=Neuchâtel| date=18 May 2014| language=de, fr| access-date=20 May 2014| archive-date=21 May 2014| archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140521031436/http://www.bfs.admin.ch/bfs/portal/de/index/themen/17/03/blank/key/2014/023.html| url-status=live}}</ref>
