|comment=The federal nationwide [[minimum wage in the United States]] is [[United States dollar|US$]]7.25 per hour.<ref name=minwage>{{Cite web |title=State Minimum Wage Laws |url=https://www.dol.gov/agencies/whd/minimum-wage/state |website=[[Wage and Hour Division]] (WHD) |publisher=[[United States Department of Labor]] |access-date=2022-01-03 |archive-date=2019-11-27 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191127215936/https://www.dol.gov/whd/minwage/america.htm |url-status=live }} Click on states on that map to see exact [[List of US states by minimum wage|minimum wage info by state]]. See bottom of page for [[District of Columbia]] and [[Territories of the United States|U.S. territories]].</ref> [[List of US states by minimum wage|States may also set a minimum]], in which case the higher of the two is controlling; some territories are exempt and have lower rates.<ref name="minwage"/> {{As of|2022|January|3|df=US}}, effective state minimum wage rates range from US$7.25 to US$16.66 per hour, with an average of about $12.00 across all minimum wage workers as of 2019.<ref name=paycor>[https://www.paycor.com/resource-center/articles/minimum-wage-by-state Minimum Wage by State 2022 Increases vs 2021 - Paycor] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220103051618/https://www.paycor.com/resource-center/articles/minimum-wage-by-state/ |date=2022-01-03 }}.</ref><ref>{{cite news |url= https://www.epi.org/minimum-wage-tracker/ |title= Minimum Wage Tracker |publisher= Economic Policy Institute |access-date= 2018-09-03 |archive-date= 2021-11-12 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20211112163931/https://www.epi.org/minimum-wage-tracker/ |url-status= live }}</ref><ref name=table>[https://www.dol.gov/agencies/whd/mw-consolidated Consolidated Minimum Wage Table] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220101180619/https://www.dol.gov/agencies/whd/mw-consolidated |date=2022-01-01 }}. From: [[Wage and Hour Division]] of the [[U.S. Department of Labor]]. See [[List of U.S. state and territory abbreviations|abbreviations list]].</ref> Local government minimum wages exist as well, the highest of which reach to $17.13 per hour.<ref>[https://www.investopedia.com/articles/investing/080515/top-5-us-cities-highest-minimum-wage.asp The Top 5 U.S. Cities With the Highest Minimum Wage] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220103152336/https://www.investopedia.com/articles/investing/080515/top-5-us-cities-highest-minimum-wage.asp |date=2022-01-03 }}. 27 June 2021. By Greg DePersio. Reviewed by Ebony Howard. [[Investopedia]].</ref>}}

